 "brief": "A cover in PETG (FDM, printed outside face down, layers along Z) for an outdoor junction box. It is 90 x 70 mm and 10 mm deep (x = -45 to 45, y = -35 to 35, z = 0 to 10); the outside is the top (z = 10) and the sides, the underside is open and sits on the box rim (the plane z = 0, a 3 mm wide band round the edge). Four M3 screws go down through the corners at x = +-39, y = +-29. The outside must stay a closed 1.6 mm skin. Someone leaning on it presses 150 N on a thumb-sized patch at the middle of the top; it must not sag more than 1.5 mm there, where a terminal block sits under it. Safety factor 2.",
